From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] CoreFoundation: build without ICU (CF_NO_ICU)

The user's call (docs/base/corefoundation.md): no ICU, whose data is
about 30 MB. With CF_NO_ICU, the locale, calendar, formatter, regular
expression and transform sources are left out (base/corefoundation/
build.sh) and the files that stay lose their ICU calls: CFString's
grapheme clusters use CF's own Grapheme_Extend bitmap (no
Extended_Pictographic, Prepend or SpacingMark: emoji ZWJ sequences are
not one cluster), localized number formatting falls back to the C
locale's, CFStringUtilities compares without collation (its non-ICU
path), CFTimeZone answers from its TZif periods and has no localized
names, CFBundle matches localizations by name, CFICUConverters.h makes
every ICU converter absent, and CFRuntime's class table leaves out the
types it doesn't build. base/corefoundation/src/nd_cflocale.c is the
CFLocale that remains: an identifier.

